  "body": "### Summary\n\nWanted by LOT-033 (#60): the pager parser rule for a current page sitting **between two ellipses, followed by a trailing text node**, is exercised by no capture (docs/lots LOT-033 spec lists it as pending).\n\n### Scope\n\nState to capture: a topic page (logged out is enough if HFR shows it) whose pager shows ellipsis, current page, ellipsis, with trailing text after the last link; anonymized, plus legacy oracle output.\n\n### Sources\n\n- LOT-033 spec (pending capture), HFR-PROTOCOL pager notes\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Anonymized capture and oracle output; row removed from the Capture backlog; LOT-033 spec updated.\n\nRules: LOT-001 kit (`tooling/fixtures/`), anonymize every free-text field, independent leak check before any push, never hand-build the state in the cloud (LESSONS 36), legacy oracle when a parser consumes it, one PR per batch of captures, the PR removes the row from the Capture backlog in `docs/LOTS.md`. Write captures need the operator approval first.\n",
