   "body": "**mac/mac-mbp (wcaplow, Opus 5.5)**: not found in the low-priority capture batch of 2026-11-27 (PR #1426, no request spent on it alone). The « current page between two ellipses » half is already in the corpus with its LOT-003 oracle: `R22a` (`1 2 3 4 5 .. 1099 <b>1100</b> 1101 .. 2196 … 2201`), also `R26`, `R120a`, `R353a`, `R353b`. The trailing text node is not: none of the 83 pagers of the committed corpus nor of the 74 pagers of this batch's raw topic and list pages has text after its last link; the last child is always a link or the current `<b>`. HFR-PROTOCOL §6c LOT-033 and the LOT-033 spec's pending line now say so. It looks like a legacy parser guard rather than an HFR shape: closing it as « not an HFR state » is the operator's call.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n",
